    },
    {
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "e3bcf98545ad66a9",
      "line_num": 177,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [
        "#bonsai",
        "#critical",
        "#deploy-blocker"
      ],
      "text": "**amd64 Sprig artifacts (8.J) \u2014 NOW A DEPLOY BLOCKER for sage.startr.cloud (escalated 2026-07-12 by the poka-yoke audit): the live target is amd64, the slim base dropped chromadb/langchain/pypdf/fpdf/whisper/embedding runtimes (baked into v2.3.2), and the ONLY recovery path \u2014 vector-chroma, rag-loaders, export-document, media-ffmpeg, backup-rclone, and every embedding/reranker/stt binary \u2014 is arm64-only. The host-arch guard (shipped this pass) correctly REFUSES them on amd64, so upgrading sage.startr.cloud leaves document search / ingestion / PDF export / local embedding / STT with no graft path. `make upgrade_gate` proves + prints the gap (section 6). DECISION (Alexander 2026-07-12): build the amd64 image + artifacts (buildx supports both arches on this machine). Done this pass: amd64 rootstock image (`make it_build_amd64`) builds green + boots natively under QEMU (uname x86_64, boot logs `host architecture: amd64`, arch guard refuses arm64 artifacts, neutral theme grafts+serves, /catalog reports host_arch+compatible); multi-arch catalog schema \u2014 `arches` is now a dict `{arch: {tag, binary_sha256}}` so an amd64 build drops in as one override per entry (same repo, `-amd64` tag, own sha); graft() overlays the host's arch; arm64 unchanged (verified). `scripts/repack-sprig-arch.sh` swaps just the arch-specific binary into the neutral-model artifact. Remaining (8.J artifact builds): the 3 recipe-having binaries need amd64 server builds \u2014 first llama-server attempt hit a real yak (llama.cpp b9859 web-UI embed step fails under static musl cross-build; needs a disable-webui fix); the 8 recipe-less artifacts need their build recipes written first (the #critical recipe gap), then amd64 builds (static ffmpeg/rclone = downloads; vector-chroma/rag/export = amd64 python-wheel closures via buildx). Mitigator: prod chroma already records ZERO collections (654 orphaned HNSW dirs), so search is already down on v2.3.2. Full status in `docs/deploy-sage-startr-cloud.md`.**\n`#bonsai` `#critical` `#deploy-blocker`\n`TODO.md:L177`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 360,
      "y": 60
    },
    {
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "55103d32d865a816",
      "line_num": 183,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [
        "#bonsai",
        "#critical"
      ],
      "text": "**Sprig artifact packaging has no reproducible recipe for 11 of 14 registry repos (surfaced 2026-07-03; two recipes added since): In-repo build scripts exist for `sprig-embedding-minilm-onnx` (`build-sprig-minilm.sh`), `sprig-reranker-bge-gguf` (`build-sprig-reranker.sh`), and `sprig-stt-whisper-base` (`build-sprig-whisper.sh`). The other 11 repos (`sprig-backup-rclone`, `sprig-browser-ml`, `sprig-code-pyodide`, `sprig-dev-svelte`, `sprig-embedding-bge-onnx`, `sprig-embedding-e5-gguf`, `sprig-embedding-e5-large-onnx`, `sprig-export-document`, `sprig-media-ffmpeg`, `sprig-rag-loaders`, `sprig-vector-chroma`) exist only as pushed blobs in an anonymous (unnamed) Docker volume on this one dev machine \u2014 `docker volume prune` or a lost machine would silently take them out with no way to regenerate (the 2026-07-05 disk-full VM corruption was a near-miss). The in-house llama/whisper build+convert harnesses are rescued at `~/sprig-rescue/`. Two separable fixes: (a) write the missing `build-sprig-*.sh` scripts so every `binary_sha256` pin is regenerable/auditable; (b) ~~give the registry a named volume~~ DONE 2026-07-12. (b) SHIPPED: the registry now uses the NAMED volume `sprig-registry-data` (Makefile `sprig_registry` + all 4 build scripts) \u2014 the poka-yoke pass found the artifacts had been living in an anonymous volume the whole time and recovered 2.7GB into the named one (the near-miss became a real find). (a) still open for 11 repos, and now doubly load-bearing: without recipes there are no amd64 builds (see the deploy-blocker item above).**\n`#bonsai` `#critical`\n`TODO.md:L183`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 360,
      "y": 150
    },
